From: Hermes <hermes@lassul.us>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Build as a module of the droid-nix app

droid-nix carries Termux:API in its own APK, whose package is not
com.termux.api, so the receiver's class name no longer follows from the
package name.

The droid-nix app sets ResultReturner's context in its own application
class, and leaves out TermuxAPIApplication and the socket listener it
starts (droid-nix's termux-api command uses am broadcast); the receiver
no longer sets the log level from its preferences.
---
 app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxAPIConstants.java | 2 +-
 app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxApiReceiver.java  | 1 -
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxAPIConstants.java b/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxAPIConstants.java
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxAPIConstants.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxAPIConstants.java
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ public class TermuxAPIConstants {
     /**
      * Termux:API Receiver name.
      */
-    public static final String TERMUX_API_RECEIVER_NAME = TERMUX_API_PACKAGE_NAME + ".TermuxApiReceiver"; // Default to "com.termux.api.TermuxApiReceiver"
+    public static final String TERMUX_API_RECEIVER_NAME = TermuxApiReceiver.class.getName(); // Default to "com.termux.api.TermuxApiReceiver"

     /** The Uri authority for Termux:API app file shares */
     public static final String TERMUX_API_FILE_SHARE_URI_AUTHORITY = TERMUX_PACKAGE_NAME + ".sharedfiles"; // Default: "com.termux.sharedfiles"
diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxApiReceiver.java b/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxApiReceiver.java
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxApiReceiver.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/termux/api/TermuxApiReceiver.java
@@ -59,7 +59,6 @@ public class TermuxApiReceiver extends BroadcastReceiver {

     @Override
     public void onReceive(Context context, Intent intent) {
-        TermuxAPIApplication.setLogConfig(context, false);
         Logger.logDebug(LOG_TAG, "Intent Received:\n" + IntentUtils.getIntentString(intent));

         try {
